                 Function.Injective.{u_3 + 1, u_1 + 1} f →\n                            Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f 0) 0 →\n                              Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f 1) 1 →\n                                (∀ (x y : S),\n                                    Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f (HAdd.hAdd.{u_3, u_3, u_3} x y))\n                                      (HAdd.hAdd.{u_1, u_1, u_1} (f x) (f y))) →\n                                  (∀ (x : S), Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f (Neg.neg.{u_3} x)) (Neg.neg.{u_1} (f x))) →\n                                    (∀ (x y : S),\n                                        Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f (HSub.hSub.{u_3, u_3, u_3} x y))\n                                          (HSub.hSub.{u_1, u_1, u_1} (f x) (f y))) →\n                                      (∀ (n : Nat) (x : S),\n                                          Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f (HSMul.hSMul.{0, u_3, u_3} n x))\n                                            (HSMul.hSMul.{0, u_1, u_1} n (f x))) →\n                                        (∀ (n : Int) (x : S),\n                                            Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f (HSMul.hSMul.{0, u_3, u_3} n x))\n                                              (HSMul.hSMul.{0, u_1, u_1} n (f x))) →\n                                          (∀ (n : Nat), Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f ↑n) ↑n) →\n                                            (∀ (n : Int), Eq.{u_1 + 1} (f ↑n) ↑n) → AddGroupWithOne.{u_3} S","unsafe":false,"value":587,"source":{"code":"/-- A type endowed with `0`, `1` and `+` is an additive group with one, if it admits an injective\nmap that preserves `0`, `1` and `+` to an additive group with one.  See note\n[reducible non-instances]. -/\nprotected abbrev addGroupWithOne {S} [Zero S] [One S] [Add S] [SMul ℕ S] [Neg S] [Sub S]\n    [SMul ℤ S] [NatCast S] [IntCast S] [AddGroupWithOne R] (f : S → R) (hf : Injective f)\n    (zero : f 0 = 0) (one : f 1 = 1) (add : ∀ x y, f (x + y) = f x + f y) (neg : ∀ x, f (-x) = -f x)\n    (sub : ∀ x y, f (x - y) = f x - f y) (nsmul : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x), f (n • x) = n • f x)\n    (zsmul : ∀ (n : ℤ) (x), f (n • x) = n • f x) (natCast : ∀ n : ℕ, f n = n)\n    (intCast : ∀ n : ℤ, f n = n) : AddGroupWithOne S :=\n  { hf.addGroup f zero add neg sub (swap nsmul) (swap zsmul),\n    hf.addMonoidWithOne f zero one add nsmul natCast with\n    intCast := Int.cast,\n    intCast_ofNat := fun n => hf (by rw [natCast, intCast, Int.cast_natCast]),\n    intCast_negSucc := fun n => hf (by rw [intCast, neg, natCast, Int.cast_negSucc] ) }","start":89,"end":102},"axioms":["propext"]}